# Admin navigation naming

## Rule

| Screen type | Label form | Examples |
|-------------|------------|----------|
| List of many records (CRUD / tables) | **Plural** | Brands, Products, Customers, Suppliers, Users, Branches, Leaves |
| Concept, tool, or process | **Singular or short phrase** | Dashboard, Inventory, Attendance, Payroll, Settings, Stock on hand |
| Nav group titles | Singular concept or short label | Catalog, Inventory, Financials, HR, Settings |

If the page is mainly a table of entities → plural. If it is a workspace or topic → singular / phrase.

## Do

- Prefer plural for entity list screens and “Add X” buttons (`Add User`, `Add Brand`)
- Keep descriptive phrases for non-lists (`Import / export`, `Roles & permissions`, `Bonuses / deductions`)
- Match route/page names to the plural entity when practical (`admin.users.*`, `Admin/Users/`)

## Don’t

- Mix singular and plural for the same kind of screen (e.g. `Leave` next to `Customers`)
- Use vague narrow labels when the screen covers more than one concern — prefer familiar terms (`Users` over `Staff` for login + employee accounts)

## People & Contacts

- Customers, Suppliers, Users (merged login + optional employee profile)
